     hostname.
  3. [1mWhich API base URL for each?[0m I only know the production one, and only as a full login URL rather than a base.

  One structural note while you answer: I'd store an [1mAPI base URL[0m per environment (e.g. [38;5;153mhttps://api.example.com[39m) and let
  callers append the path, rather than storing the full [38;5;153m/login[39m URL. Since you've said more config is coming, that keeps
  the second and third endpoints from each needing their own environment table. [38;5;153mapp.js[39m would then build its URL from
  [38;5;153mAppSettings.apiBaseUrl[39m, and the existing [38;5;153mAPI_ENDPOINT[39m constant becomes a derived value there.

